**What changed:** I reordered `fom_iterate` in `src/fom_ops.c`. It now computes each `t1` row right after the `t0` rows that feed it, keeping intermediate values in registers. Each floating-point sum is done in the same order as before, so results should be bit-identical.

Since the gain is under the stopping threshold, the next round can probably end the pipeline.

